  "result": "I fixed the bug: `click.IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True).convert('0', None, None)` now returns 1. `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` gives 45 passed and 2 skipped.\n\nThe cause was in `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py`). The caller passes `dir=1` for the min bound and `dir=-1` for the max bound, meaning the direction to move into the range. `_clamp` subtracted `dir` instead of adding it, so open bounds moved outward. It now returns `bound + dir`.\n\nI added four cases to the clamp parametrize list at the top of `tests/test_types.py`. They cover an open min bound (`\"0\"` and `\"-5\"` both give 1) and an open max bound (`\"5\"` and `\"9\"` both give 4). I didn't run the new cases against the old code to confirm they fail there.",
